import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'boulder-control':('Hill giant: correct path, unfavorable teleport outcome','The original counts the throwing giant itself as an obstacle and estimates zero danger. Its boulder still removes 18 HP. The helper correction recognizes a clear shot, but the chosen teleport costs 2 mana and still takes 29 HP in this seeded recording. Correct recognition is not uniform safety.'),
 'clear-path':('Storm giant: clear shot and successful escape','Recognizing the clear path changes the giant\'s threat estimate. The correction uses a scroll, moves behind a wall and retains 130 HP instead of losing 54 HP. The independent per-spell correction also changes this area-attack case, but does not repair the caster-origin path itself.'),
 'boulder-blocked':('Control: actual mold blocks the boulder','A real visible yellow mold stands between the hill giant and Rogue. Both versions reject the shot; the native boulder does not damage the Rogue. The correction ignores only the caster, not genuine intermediate creatures.'),
 'blocked':('Control: storm giant behind a real mold','The path remains blocked and the helper-only correction leaves the original action/damage unchanged. The separate mixed-spell defect still underestimates the giant\'s area attacks; this helper patch does not include that correction.'),
 'ball-control':('Outcome control: patriarch area spell','The caster-origin path is recognized correctly after the helper change, but this caster\'s selected escape and native resource/damage result stay unchanged.'),
 'direct-control':('Outcome control: orc shaman direct attack','The caster-origin path changes, but the direct-attack escape choice, mana use and native damage result are unchanged.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','per-spell-only','both','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text();frames=[json.loads(l[6:]) for l in raw.splitlines() if l.startswith('FRAME ')]
  assert len(frames)==3
  match=re.search(r'OUTCOME (.*)',raw);outcome={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])}
  geometry={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',re.search(r'GEOMETRY (.*)',raw)[1])}
  danger=int(re.search(r'DANGER current=(\d+)',raw)[1])
  assert frames[0]['hp']-frames[2]['hp']==outcome['hp_lost']
  item[phase]={'frames':frames,'outcome':outcome,'geometry':geometry,'danger':danger,'raw':raw}
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The caster is not an obstacle to its own shot</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:42px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.hp{font-size:40px;font-weight:750}.path{font-weight:700}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:32px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native caster/player paths, escape choice and scheduled spell</p><h1>The Borg counts the throwing giant as an obstacle to its own boulder</h1><p>A Rogue sees a hill giant six squares away, with no creature or wall between them. The original path check stops on the giant itself and rates its boulder at zero danger. A native scheduled boulder still hits for 18 HP. The correction recognizes the clear shot; it then spends 2 mana teleporting but remains exposed and takes 29 HP in this recording.</p><p>This fixes a false blocked-shot assessment. The unfavorable hill-giant outcome remains visible; no uniform safety improvement is claimed. The clear-path storm-giant example shows another consequence: the correction uses a scroll, moves behind a wall and avoids the scheduled spell. Actual intervening creatures and walls remain obstacles.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><label for="variant">Compare the original with:</label><br><select id="variant"><option value="after">Proposed fix: exclude the starting caster</option><option value="per-spell-only">Alternative: only assess each spell separately</option><option value="both">Diagnostic: both independent corrections</option></select><br><button data-step="0">Start</button><button data-step="1">Show escape choice</button><button data-step="2">Show scheduled spell</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><p class="path"></p><div class="hp"></div><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2 id="variant-title"></h2><p class="path"></p><div class="hp"></div><p class="stats"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>Player-origin paths, starting-point endpoints and walls retain their existing results. A real mold still blocks the boulder, while a creature at the final target remains a valid endpoint. Two complete intermediate-monster logs are unchanged; four native action/resource/damage comparisons are unchanged. Some diagnostic path fields correctly change even when the selected native action does not.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Rogue level 20, 130 HP/121 mana, depth 38, seed 1000, known Phase Door spell and one scroll, constructed Intelligence/arena setup. The real stock monster spell lists keep their native order. The helper-only source changes one obstruction check, retaining the separate mixed-spell classification defect.</p><p>Production danger and escape routines choose. Actual spell/book or scroll keys are validated and executed natively. One scheduled valid native spell effect follows only with actual range and terrain access; the real active-monster context supplies spell power. This does not run monster AI spell selection/frequency/failure or all player fallback/world turns.</p><p>Native damage, saving throws, spell/scroll cost and movement are not substituted. Different selected actions naturally consume different random draws; no RNG is reset. Danger estimates are heuristics, not HP predictions. The shown Phase Door spells succeed despite a native 5% failure chance. No extra enemy action, death, encounter frequency or overall survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output and path queries</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Compared</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/279">issue279</a>. Independently found in the clear-path control for <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/64">CBUG-0048 / issue64</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=2;const select=document.getElementById('scenario'),variant=document.getElementById('variant');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;document.getElementById('variant-title').textContent=variant.options[variant.selectedIndex].text;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared',variant.value]]){let d=c[phase],f=d.frames[step],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.path').textContent=`Path test before the choice: caster's shot ${d.geometry.caster_clear?'clear':'blocked'}.`;p.querySelector('.hp').textContent=`${f.hp} / ${f.max_hp} HP`;p.querySelector('.stats').textContent=`Mana: ${f.mana}. Phase Door scrolls: ${f.scrolls}. Position: (${f.x}, ${f.y}). Borg danger estimate: ${d.danger}.`;p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===0?'Before the escape choice.':step===1?(d.outcome.escape?'Uses the requested teleport; recorded position shown above.':'Requests no escape.'):(d.outcome.cast?`The scheduled native spell executes; this recording loses ${d.outcome.hp_lost} HP.`:'No spell is scheduled: the caster no longer has a terrain-clear path or range.');document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}let a=c.before.outcome,b=c[variant.value].outcome;document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='boulder-control'&&variant.value!=='per-spell-only'?'Unfavorable outcome retained: correction spends 2 mana and loses 29 HP, versus 18 HP originally. Correct shot recognition does not guarantee a safer teleport.':select.value==='boulder-control'?'The independent per-spell alternative still falsely blocks the caster-origin shot and leaves this outcome unchanged.':select.value==='boulder-blocked'?'Unchanged real obstruction: the mold still blocks the boulder; no native player damage.':a.hp_after===b.hp_after&&a.scrolls_spent===b.scrolls_spent&&a.mana_spent===b.mana_spent?'Native action, resource use and damage are unchanged; path-query results are shown separately.':`Recorded final health: ${a.hp_after} → ${b.hp_after} HP. Resource costs remain visible above.`;for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=2;draw()});variant.addEventListener('change',draw);for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
